.TH REGOLITH-INPUTD 8 "August 2026" "Regolith Linux" "System Manager Manual"
.SH NAME
regolith-inputd \- synchronize input settings between desktop backends and Sway
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B regolith-inputd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B regolith-inputd
is a D-Bus daemon that keeps supported desktop input settings aligned with Sway.
It selects the GNOME or COSMIC input backend from the current desktop
environment and applies input changes to the running Sway session.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/regolith-init-inputd.service
User service used to start the daemon for supported Regolith Wayland sessions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sway (1),
.BR systemd (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Regolith Linux contributors
